-- title:
--   Zeta1 Bound
-- statement:
--   **The concrete first cascade value is bounded by the main formal error.**
--
--   Under the cascade hypotheses, suppose `nu` satisfies the coarse induction bound and `sigma` is exactly `cascadeSigma params k nu`. Then the concrete first cascade value is absorbed by the public error envelope:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{cascadeZeta1}(\mathrm{params},\varepsilon,\sigma)\le
--   \operatorname{mainFormalError}(\mathrm{params},k,\varepsilon).
--   $$
--
--   The proof dispatches the exceptional $(k,m)=(1,1)$ branch separately and uses the general bound otherwise. This is the first public scalar bound in the final cascade.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.zeta1_bound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/ScalarBounds/CascadeBounds/SigmaZeta1.lean#L415-L448

